{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tn6tgTz4XodqGmE2bKZJ3N","type":"tool_result","content":"80\t\n81\t#: Truncation sentinel. Inserted at the truncation point so audit\n82\t#: consumers can detect that the original Codex output exceeded the\n83\t#: cap. The sentinel itself is plain ASCII and contains no secrets.\n84\t_TRUNCATION_MARKER: str = (\n85\t    \"\\n\\n[CODEX-OUTPUT-TRUNCATED-AT-256KB-PER-_MAX_REDACT_INPUT_BYTES]\\n\"\n86\t)\n87\t\n88\t\n89\tdef redact(text: str) -> str:\n90\t    \"\"\"Redact secrets + PII from a Codex output string.\n91\t\n92\t    Single-pass invariant per R1 S-Sec-1: calls ONE\n93\t    ``secret_patterns.scan_and_redact(text, patterns=ALL_PATTERNS)``\n94\t    invocation. NEVER chains pattern subsets.\n95\t\n96\t    Args:\n97\t        text: Codex output (UTF-8 string).\n98\t\n99\t    Returns:\n100\t        Redacted text with all matched secrets / PII replaced by\n101\t        their canonical labels (e.g. ``[REDACTED-OPENAI-KEY]``,\n102\t        ``[REDACTED-CPF]``). Empty string in → empty string out.\n103\t\n104\t    NEVER raises. Performance bounded by ``scan_and_redact``'s\n105\t    ``budget_seconds=0.5`` default.\n106\t    \"\"\"\n107\t    if not text or not isinstance(text, str):\n108\t        return \"\"\n109\t\n110\t    # Truncate at the hard cap. The sentinel makes this visible to\n111\t    # audit consumers so they don't assume a clean Codex completion.\n112\t    if len(text.encode(\"utf-8\")) > _MAX_REDACT_INPUT_BYTES:\n113\t        # Encode → truncate bytes → decode safely (replace surrogates).\n114\t        truncated = text.encode(\"utf-8\")[:_MAX_REDACT_INPUT_BYTES]\n115\t        text = truncated.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\") + _TRUNCATION_MARKER\n116\t\n117\t    # SINGLE-PASS scan_and_redact — R1 S-Sec-1 invariant.\n118\t    # Patterns default to ALL_PATTERNS (which is SECRETS + PII).\n119\t    redacted, _findings = _patterns.scan_and_redact(text)\n120\t    return redacted\n121\t\n122\t\n123\tdef redact_with_findings(text: str) -> Tuple[str, List[_patterns.Finding]]:\n124\t    \"\"\"Redact + return findings for audit emission.\n125\t\n126\t    Same single-pass guarantee as ``redact()``. Returns the redacted\n127\t    text alongside the list of ``Finding`` objects so callers can:\n128\t\n129\t    - emit ``finding_count_by_family`` to the audit log (Sec MF-3\n130\t      whitelist);\n131\t    - assert in tests that specific patterns matched (e.g. PEM-with-\n132\t      embedded-CPF detects BOTH overlap families in a single pass).\n133\t\n134\t    Args:\n135\t        text: Codex output.\n136\t\n137\t    Returns:\n138\t        ``(redacted_text, findings)`` tuple. Findings list is empty\n139\t        on no matches. NEVER raises.\n140\t    \"\"\"\n141\t    if not text or not isinstance(text, str):\n142\t        return \"\", []\n143\t\n144\t    if len(text.encode(\"utf-8\")) > _MAX_REDACT_INPUT_BYTES:\n145\t        truncated = text.encode(\"utf-8\")[:_MAX_REDACT_INPUT_BYTES]\n146\t        text = truncated.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\") + _TRUNCATION_MARKER\n147\t\n148\t    redacted, findings = _patterns.scan_and_redact(text)\n149\t    return redacted, findings\n150\t\n151\t\n152\tdef family_ids() -> List[str]:\n153\t    \"\"\"Expose the canonical family_id list for audit-emit allowlist tests.\n154\t\n155\t    Returns the family_id values from the canonical ``ALL_PATTERNS``\n156\t    constant. Tests pin the count to detect drift (any new pattern\n157\t    family added must be reflected in audit-emit Sec MF-3 allowlist).\n158\t    \"\"\"\n159\t    return _patterns.family_ids()\n160\t\n161\t\n162\tdef is_single_pass_invariant() -> bool:\n163\t    \"\"\"ABI conformance helper — declares single-pass guarantee.\n164\t\n165\t    Used by the ABI conformance test\n166\t    (``test_codex_egress_redact.py:TestSinglePassInvariant``) to\n167\t    confirm this module hasn't been refactored into a chain. The\n168\t    helper inspects the source of ``redact()`` and asserts:\n169\t\n170\t    - Exactly ONE call to ``_patterns.scan_and_redact``.\n171\t    - NO calls to ``_patterns.scan`` followed by ``_patterns.redact``.\n172\t\n173\t    Returns True iff invariant holds.\n174\t    \"\"\"\n175\t    # The conformance test re-implements this check via AST parsing\n176\t    # of the module source for forensic clarity. This helper exists\n177\t    # to make the invariant declaratively visible to readers; the\n178\t    # test itself does the verification.\n179\t    return True\n180\t\n181\t\n182\tdef redact_outgoing(text: str) -> str:\n183\t    \"\"\"PLAN-084 Wave 0.5 (R1 Sec-P0-2 + R2 CODEX-P0-1 expansion).\n184\t\n185\t    Mirror of redact() but for OUTGOING prompts (framework → Codex/external\n186\t    LLM). Applies the same pattern families as redact(), but additionally\n187\t    scrubs:\n188\t      - framework GPG fingerprints (sentinel-signers.txt content)\n189\t      - audit-log HMAC keys (if accidentally embedded in evidence quotes)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f36400ef-26f6-4b31-b68a-075981f68fdb","uuid":"c8a00c61-3845-41b7-a4e8-e8fc3545610c","timestamp":"2026-11-13T17:40:23.817Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/hooks/_lib/codex_egress_redact.py","content":"\n#: Truncation sentinel. Inserted at the truncation point so audit\n#: consumers can detect that the original Codex output exceeded the\n#: cap. The sentinel itself is plain ASCII and contains no secrets.\n_TRUNCATION_MARKER: str = (\n    \"\\n\\n[CODEX-OUTPUT-TRUNCATED-AT-256KB-PER-_MAX_REDACT_INPUT_BYTES]\\n\"\n)\n\n\ndef redact(text: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Redact secrets + PII from a Codex output string.\n\n    Single-pass invariant per R1 S-Sec-1: calls ONE\n    ``secret_patterns.scan_and_redact(text, patterns=ALL_PATTERNS)``\n    invocation. NEVER chains pattern subsets.\n\n    Args:\n        text: Codex output (UTF-8 string).\n\n    Returns:\n        Redacted text with all matched secrets / PII replaced by\n        their canonical labels (e.g. ``[REDACTED-OPENAI-KEY]``,\n        ``[REDACTED-CPF]``). Empty string in → empty string out.\n\n    NEVER raises. Performance bounded by ``scan_and_redact``'s\n    ``budget_seconds=0.5`` default.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not text or not isinstance(text, str):\n        return \"\"\n\n    # Truncate at the hard cap. The sentinel makes this visible to\n    # audit consumers so they don't assume a clean Codex completion.\n    if len(text.encode(\"utf-8\")) > _MAX_REDACT_INPUT_BYTES:\n        # Encode → truncate bytes → decode safely (replace surrogates).\n        truncated = text.encode(\"utf-8\")[:_MAX_REDACT_INPUT_BYTES]\n        text = truncated.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\") + _TRUNCATION_MARKER\n\n    # SINGLE-PASS scan_and_redact — R1 S-Sec-1 invariant.\n    # Patterns default to ALL_PATTERNS (which is SECRETS + PII).\n    redacted, _findings = _patterns.scan_and_redact(text)\n    return redacted\n\n\ndef redact_with_findings(text: str) -> Tuple[str, List[_patterns.Finding]]:\n    \"\"\"Redact + return findings for audit emission.\n\n    Same single-pass guarantee as ``redact()``. Returns the redacted\n    text alongside the list of ``Finding`` objects so callers can:\n\n    - emit ``finding_count_by_family`` to the audit log (Sec MF-3\n      whitelist);\n    - assert in tests that specific patterns matched (e.g. PEM-with-\n      embedded-CPF detects BOTH overlap families in a single pass).\n\n    Args:\n        text: Codex output.\n\n    Returns:\n        ``(redacted_text, findings)`` tuple. Findings list is empty\n        on no matches. NEVER raises.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not text or not isinstance(text, str):\n        return \"\", []\n\n    if len(text.encode(\"utf-8\")) > _MAX_REDACT_INPUT_BYTES:\n        truncated = text.encode(\"utf-8\")[:_MAX_REDACT_INPUT_BYTES]\n        text = truncated.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\") + _TRUNCATION_MARKER\n\n    redacted, findings = _patterns.scan_and_redact(text)\n    return redacted, findings\n\n\ndef family_ids() -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Expose the canonical family_id list for audit-emit allowlist tests.\n\n    Returns the family_id values from the canonical ``ALL_PATTERNS``\n    constant. Tests pin the count to detect drift (any new pattern\n    family added must be reflected in audit-emit Sec MF-3 allowlist).\n    \"\"\"\n    return _patterns.family_ids()\n\n\ndef is_single_pass_invariant() -> bool:\n    \"\"\"ABI conformance helper — declares single-pass guarantee.\n\n    Used by the ABI conformance test\n    (``test_codex_egress_redact.py:TestSinglePassInvariant``) to\n    confirm this module hasn't been refactored into a chain. The\n    helper inspects the source of ``redact()`` and asserts:\n\n    - Exactly ONE call to ``_patterns.scan_and_redact``.\n    - NO calls to ``_patterns.scan`` followed by ``_patterns.redact``.\n\n    Returns True iff invariant holds.\n    \"\"\"\n    # The conformance test re-implements this check via AST parsing\n    # of the module source for forensic clarity. This helper exists\n    # to make the invariant declaratively visible to readers; the\n    # test itself does the verification.\n    return True\n\n\ndef redact_outgoing(text: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"PLAN-084 Wave 0.5 (R1 Sec-P0-2 + R2 CODEX-P0-1 expansion).\n\n    Mirror of redact() but for OUTGOING prompts (framework → Codex/external\n    LLM). Applies the same pattern families as redact(), but additionally\n    scrubs:\n      - framework GPG fingerprints (sentinel-signers.txt content)\n      - audit-log HMAC keys (if accidentally embedded in evidence quotes)","numLines":110,"startLine":80,"totalLines":314}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Tn6tgTz4XodqGmE2bKZJ3N","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
