mance bounded by budget_seconds=0.5\". Also, a timeout on the original-text frame is logged only at DEBUG, so callers cannot see that detection fell back to NFKC-only.\n   - Fix: document that the budget is per frame, or split one budget across both frames, and have codex_egress_redact report the timeout.\n4. _lib/plan_paths.py:13-23 (used by policy_preprocessors.py:315-319 and check_plan_edit.py:240).\n   - What goes wrong: compared with the old `PLAN-\\d{3}-[a-z0-9-]+\\.md`, the new pattern also rejects names with `--`, a trailing `-`, or non-ASCII digits. Such files stop being plan-gated. CHANGELOG [1.4.4] (line 332) mentions only the FOLLOWUP widening. check_budget.py:155 still uses the permissive pattern, so the two consumers classify these names differently. The docstring says paths are \"normalized\", but only `\\` becomes `/`: there is no folding of `.`/`..` or of letter case. That gap existed before this change.\n   - Fix: add a CHANGELOG line for the narrowing, and use plan_paths in check_budget.py.\n5. _lib/model_currency.py:7-16.\n   - What goes wrong: the family pattern has no `claude-fable-*`. Fable is accepted only as the exact legacy ids `claude-fable-5` / `claude-fable-5-1`, and only when explicit_models is None. A newer Fable id needs an explicit list entry. This is consistent with the declared design but easy to miss.\n   - Fix: add a sentence to ADR-149 or the docstring.\n6. _lib/federation/_server_parts/__init__.py:4.\n   - What goes wrong: a second docstring-like string literal that does nothing.\n   - Fix: fold it into the module docstring.","decision":"GO","sentence":"The declared conditions this payload touches (4, 5, 7 and 9) all hold against the candidate code, the moved federation and policy code behaves as it did before, the secret- and PII-redaction offset fixes are correct and fail toward over-redaction, and I found no P0 or new P1, only six P2 follow-ups."},"ttft_ms":5645,"type":"result","duration_ms":563793,"uuid":"f7282666-1193-423e